<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2646" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">an-năto</span></b>  (better <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adn-</span></b> ), āre, v. n.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To swim to</i> or <i>toward</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ei insulae crocodili non adnatant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 25, 38, § 93</span></i>
			; Jan here reads <i>adnant;</i>
			<i><span class="en">Sil. 10,
				610</span></i>.—With <i>ad</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad manum hominis adnatare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					9, 29, 46, § 87</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">9, 10, 12,
				§ 38</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To swim along by</i> or <i>by the side
				of</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">comes lateri adnatat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Agam. 452</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
